WEBVTT

00:04.004 --> 00:05.338
Mitsuoka!

00:05.422 --> 00:06.548
Noren!

00:06.631 --> 00:08.299
Wait up!

00:08.383 --> 00:11.302
Tell us more
about what you said back there!

00:12.470 --> 00:13.722
Wait!

00:14.848 --> 00:16.641
Looks like we managed to lose them.

00:18.018 --> 00:19.853
All right, now.

00:19.936 --> 00:21.187
Why?

00:21.271 --> 00:22.188
Sorry!

00:22.772 --> 00:26.025
The club activity I was really looking
forward to got totally wrecked...

00:26.109 --> 00:30.447
and before I knew it, all my
built-up stress completely exploded.

00:30.530 --> 00:32.532
I know I messed up.

00:32.615 --> 00:34.034
Sorry.

00:34.993 --> 00:38.413
But hey, Juzo, doesn't this
technically mean mission accomplished?

00:38.496 --> 00:39.664
The hell it does!

00:39.748 --> 00:42.500
Marrying a kid
the same age as my daughter?

00:42.584 --> 00:43.918
I'd rather die!

00:44.502 --> 00:47.464
Please! I know it's selfish...

00:47.547 --> 00:50.925
but could you pretend
to be my boyfriend for a while?

00:51.009 --> 00:52.051
Huh?

00:52.135 --> 00:54.888
Look, if people think
I already have a boyfriend,

00:54.971 --> 00:57.932
then stuff like what just happened
should calm down a little!

00:58.016 --> 00:59.225
Please!

01:02.103 --> 01:03.480
Fine.

01:04.272 --> 01:06.483
But this is strictly pretend, got it?

02:37.031 --> 02:40.952
SATURDAY, MAY 2ND

02:41.536 --> 02:42.453
Hey!

02:42.537 --> 02:44.247
Go buy us some bread!

02:44.330 --> 02:46.708
Oh, so this is how it goes.

02:46.791 --> 02:48.668
You listening to me or what?

02:49.544 --> 02:51.880
From now on, you either
run errands for us every day,

02:51.963 --> 02:53.923
or you back off from Noren Mitsuoka.

02:54.007 --> 02:55.425
Pick one.

02:55.508 --> 02:56.634
What kind of choice is that?

03:01.306 --> 03:02.473
Don't let him get away!

03:02.557 --> 03:04.434
Beating them down would be easy...

03:04.517 --> 03:09.272
but I'm not about to do something that
childish and get myself suspended over it.

03:13.151 --> 03:14.402
- Hey!
- We're on the third floor!

03:15.361 --> 03:16.654
What the...

03:22.452 --> 03:23.661
My apologies.

03:33.046 --> 03:34.255
Did you hear?

03:34.339 --> 03:36.716
Those two are apparently going out!

03:36.799 --> 03:40.053
Yeah, and because of that,
a bunch of guys have it out for him.

03:40.136 --> 03:41.471
Yikes!

03:41.554 --> 03:42.430
Poor guy.

03:43.514 --> 03:46.434
I said I'd do it
as long as it was just pretend,

03:46.517 --> 03:48.895
but is this what it's gonna be like
the whole time?

03:48.978 --> 03:50.939
What a pain!

03:51.022 --> 03:52.440
- Rough day, Oga.
- Huh?

03:52.523 --> 03:55.193
Is it true you're dating Noren?

03:55.276 --> 03:56.903
Takada and Baba...

03:56.986 --> 04:00.240
Seriously, though, nice job
getting away from those guys!

04:00.323 --> 04:01.324
You were watching?

04:01.407 --> 04:03.451
And all you did was watch?

04:03.534 --> 04:05.870
I mean, what were we supposed to do?

04:05.954 --> 04:07.705
Go get a teacher or something!

04:07.789 --> 04:11.084
It felt like you would handle it somehow.

04:11.167 --> 04:13.753
And you did, so what's the problem?

04:13.836 --> 04:14.587
Hey!

04:14.671 --> 04:15.588
Though...

04:16.172 --> 04:18.841
honestly, it could get
way worse from here.

04:19.425 --> 04:20.593
Huh?

04:21.177 --> 04:25.265
Our school's a pretty famous
mega-school, y'know.

04:25.348 --> 04:28.476
There are elite guys all over the place.

04:29.018 --> 04:30.812
And not just that.

04:30.895 --> 04:33.231
Among the upper crust,

04:33.314 --> 04:36.067
there's an especially scary group
of them called the "Unicorns."

04:36.150 --> 04:39.612
They've got the looks,
the personality, the whole package.

04:39.696 --> 04:42.490
And on top of that, every single one
of them has top-tier talent

04:42.573 --> 04:45.118
and crazy charisma
in some field or another.

04:45.201 --> 04:48.746
Rumor is, all of them
are after Noren, too.

04:49.330 --> 04:51.958
So, chances are,
they'll come after you sooner or later!

04:52.041 --> 04:53.376
And when that happens...

04:53.459 --> 04:54.585
well, good luck!

04:54.669 --> 04:55.503
Hey!

04:57.505 --> 04:59.716
You really oughta quit, don't you think?

04:59.799 --> 05:01.467
This "fake boyfriend" thing, I mean.

05:01.551 --> 05:03.094
- Huh?
- Boss...

05:03.177 --> 05:06.014
you've got no intention
of marrying Noren, right?

05:06.097 --> 05:07.807
Obviously not!

05:07.890 --> 05:10.643
Then there's no reason to keep this up.

05:10.727 --> 05:12.812
I do feel bad for her, but...

05:14.355 --> 05:16.899
And I've got one more
annoying update for you.

05:16.983 --> 05:17.942
What?

05:18.526 --> 05:22.739
It's about Mitsuoka Pharmaceuticals' wasp
research and their antiaging drug.

05:22.822 --> 05:25.950
Apparently, the underworld
is after that secret, too.

05:26.034 --> 05:29.871
But they can't just take it
with threats or brute force.

05:29.954 --> 05:31.873
So, there's talk that other organizations

05:31.956 --> 05:35.376
might send in
elite middle schooler operatives

05:35.460 --> 05:36.961
to go undercover.

05:37.045 --> 05:40.631
All with the aim of becoming
Noren Mitsuoka's future husband.

05:41.466 --> 05:43.885
Meaning from here on out,
she's basically gonna be fought over

05:43.968 --> 05:46.387
by top-tier guys
from both sides of society.

05:46.471 --> 05:50.391
Unicorns, assassin agents, the whole deal.

05:50.933 --> 05:53.019
Boss, you planning
to throw your hat in that ring, too?

05:57.899 --> 05:58.900
Huh?

05:58.983 --> 06:02.779
Yeah, so, you don't have to pretend
to be my boyfriend anymore.

06:02.862 --> 06:06.074
Looks like it's causing you
a ton of trouble. Sorry.

06:06.157 --> 06:07.909
Yeah, but then...

06:07.992 --> 06:11.287
I mean, this is really something
I should deal with myself anyway.

06:11.370 --> 06:14.332
I'll stop showing up at Home Ec Club.

06:14.415 --> 06:17.335
But hey, you should
still come by for ramen.

06:17.960 --> 06:20.463
I might vent to you
once in a while, though.

06:22.924 --> 06:23.841
Oh!

06:23.925 --> 06:25.802
On a date? Perfect timing!

06:26.385 --> 06:29.806
Quit running away already, Ogami.

06:29.889 --> 06:32.850
Nobody's okay with this, y'know.

06:32.934 --> 06:35.353
A gloomy loser like you
being her boyfriend?

06:35.436 --> 06:39.107
He's not my boyfriend anymore!
Can you quit this stupid crap already?

06:39.190 --> 06:41.067
Huh? Really?

06:41.150 --> 06:42.902
Then go out with me!

06:42.985 --> 06:44.403
What? No, thanks!

06:44.987 --> 06:47.073
Nobody asked you
to barge in here, so go to hell!

06:47.156 --> 06:48.783
Look, I'm not messing around!

06:48.866 --> 06:51.619
I'm strong, okay? I can protect you!

06:52.328 --> 06:54.705
I didn't ask! So, back off already!

06:54.789 --> 06:56.124
Aw, don't be so cold!

06:56.791 --> 06:59.127
No. We're still together.

06:59.210 --> 07:01.087
So, keep your hands off my girl.

07:01.754 --> 07:02.630
Now get lost.

07:02.713 --> 07:03.798
- Huh?
- The hell?

07:03.881 --> 07:05.925
Wait, what? You're marrying her?

07:06.008 --> 07:08.511
Like hell I am!
We're just keeping the act going!

07:09.095 --> 07:10.847
Still, why, though?

07:10.930 --> 07:12.557
No reason.

07:13.307 --> 07:14.308
What?

07:14.392 --> 07:17.603
If I had to say, it's because
every damn kid keeps going,

07:17.687 --> 07:19.439
"No, don't," "It's fine" all the time!

07:20.189 --> 07:22.400
And us old guys?
We're stubborn, that's why.

07:22.483 --> 07:24.485
If the alternative
is letting kids worry about me,

07:24.569 --> 07:26.362
then fine, I'll be
a meddling pain in the ass.

07:26.446 --> 07:27.572
I don't care who comes along.

07:27.655 --> 07:30.366
If they're bad news,
I'll swat every last one of 'em away!

07:30.450 --> 07:32.660
What're you muttering about?

07:32.743 --> 07:34.745
I spar with grown men at the gym.

07:34.829 --> 07:36.956
You oughta think
about who you're mouthing off to

07:37.039 --> 07:38.666
before you try acting cool!

07:42.503 --> 07:48.968
I'm not saying I totally disagree with the
whole "men should protect women" thing,

07:49.051 --> 07:49.927
but for now...

07:50.553 --> 07:53.097
maybe you should spend
a little more time training.

07:54.974 --> 07:56.350
Ogami?

08:00.730 --> 08:02.482
Ogami, um...

08:03.316 --> 08:06.068
All right. I'll keep playing boyfriend
a little longer.

08:06.152 --> 08:09.405
I don't wanna eat good ramen and then
have to listen to you complain afterward.

08:10.364 --> 08:11.532
Thanks.

08:12.116 --> 08:15.203
But, that
"Keep your hands off my girl" line...

08:15.286 --> 08:17.580
Sorry, but wow, that was a huge turnoff.

08:17.663 --> 08:20.291
No middle schooler talks like that.

08:21.959 --> 08:22.877
So...

08:23.794 --> 08:26.756
that's Noren Mitsuoka and her boyfriend.

08:28.132 --> 08:31.844
Though, with those moves, he kind of seems
like he might be in the same line of work.

08:35.348 --> 08:37.808
He may be tougher than I expected

08:38.518 --> 08:40.978
as a romantic rival on this job.

09:05.836 --> 09:07.171
Impressive.

09:07.964 --> 09:10.341
At your age, and with skills that sharp.

09:10.841 --> 09:13.844
You're a once-in-a-generation talent
for our organization.

09:13.928 --> 09:15.137
Thanks.

09:16.430 --> 09:18.140
Now for your next assignment.

09:19.141 --> 09:24.438
Infiltrate Noren Mitsuoka's middle school
and become her fiancé.

09:25.022 --> 09:28.067
I'm counting on you, Baby-Face Baby.

09:31.112 --> 09:33.030
Hey, Ogami...

09:33.948 --> 09:36.617
- Aren't you, like, secretly super strong?
- Huh?

09:37.201 --> 09:38.286
No way.

09:38.369 --> 09:41.956
I've never been in a fight in my life.

09:42.540 --> 09:44.417
Really?

09:44.500 --> 09:48.296
Because the guy you scared off
the other day looked pretty tough to me.

09:48.379 --> 09:51.549
That was just a fluke, or,
I dunno, for all he looked the part...

09:52.550 --> 09:54.093
he was basically normal.

09:54.176 --> 09:55.595
"Normal"?

09:55.678 --> 09:59.348
So, that means you do know
what "not normal" is like?

09:59.432 --> 10:01.434
No, I mean, I don't know.

10:01.976 --> 10:04.061
Boss is getting grilled
by a middle schooler!

10:04.729 --> 10:07.565
Well, whatever.
This is just pretend dating anyway,

10:07.648 --> 10:10.443
so I'm not gonna tell you
you can't keep secrets or anything.

10:10.985 --> 10:13.696
But speaking of this
"fake boyfriend" thing...

10:13.779 --> 10:17.116
my dad randomly sent me
something yesterday.

10:19.744 --> 10:21.203
A fountain pen?

10:22.622 --> 10:24.332
What makes zero sense is

10:24.415 --> 10:27.460
he told me to give this to Ogami,
the guy I'm dating right now.

10:28.044 --> 10:29.295
Why?

10:29.378 --> 10:30.671
No clue.

10:34.508 --> 10:36.344
Isn't he kinda hot?

10:36.427 --> 10:37.845
He's so tall!

10:38.471 --> 10:40.181
Look at how long his legs are!

10:40.264 --> 10:41.932
Check out his physique!

10:42.683 --> 10:45.561
Okay, class, I'd like to introduce
our transfer student.

10:47.730 --> 10:48.689
Boss!

10:49.190 --> 10:50.232
Yeah.

10:50.775 --> 10:52.902
A transfer student at a time like this...

10:52.985 --> 10:54.403
And that presence...

10:54.904 --> 10:56.989
So, one really did show up.

10:57.573 --> 11:02.578
They sent in another pro
to become Noren's fiancé.

11:03.079 --> 11:05.122
This is Shin Kohazame.

11:06.666 --> 11:08.459
- Hell yes! A hottie!
- Everyone, be nice to him.

11:08.542 --> 11:11.545
Man, what a difference from Oga!
No, seriously, it's not even a contest!

11:12.129 --> 11:14.882
Now then, why don't you
give us a quick introduction?

11:18.969 --> 11:20.388
Afu?

11:23.557 --> 11:25.309
Duck?

11:36.570 --> 11:40.282
Wow, he's so nervous,
he completely choked.

11:40.366 --> 11:45.788
Um, okay then, for now,
why don't you sit next to Mitsuoka?

11:48.958 --> 11:51.377
Uh, nice to meet you.

11:54.797 --> 11:55.631
Huh?

11:57.633 --> 11:58.634
She's...

11:58.717 --> 12:00.594
She's so cute!

12:00.678 --> 12:03.597
Her picture did not do her justice!

12:03.681 --> 12:04.640
This is bad!

12:04.723 --> 12:07.393
I'm so nervous, I can barely even talk!

12:07.476 --> 12:10.312
There's no way
I can flirt with a girl this cute!

12:11.105 --> 12:12.815
But it's a job, so I have to!

12:12.898 --> 12:14.859
If I'm gonna talk without freaking out,

12:14.942 --> 12:17.445
I've got no choice
but to put that in my mouth!

12:18.988 --> 12:19.989
Huh?

12:20.489 --> 12:21.323
A letter?

12:21.407 --> 12:22.867
I LIKE YOU
I'LL BE WAITING AFTER SCHOOL

12:22.950 --> 12:24.076
What?!

12:24.160 --> 12:27.163
Did I really just get the sloppiest
love-letter approach ever?

12:31.167 --> 12:35.004
Jeez, when you're hot, people really
let you get away with anything, huh?

12:37.590 --> 12:40.134
A letter and then
an instant meet-up request.

12:40.217 --> 12:42.219
You want me there with you?

12:42.303 --> 12:43.554
Honestly, that'd help.

12:43.637 --> 12:45.764
That's the whole point
of the "fake boyfriend" thing.

12:45.848 --> 12:47.933
I knew you had a boyfriend.

12:48.017 --> 12:51.687
But if you bring him with you,
that does make this way harder. Jeez.

12:51.770 --> 12:52.521
Huh?

12:53.230 --> 12:57.318
Wait, that's Kohazame's voice,
but the vibe is completely different.

12:58.652 --> 13:00.905
No, hang on, what the heck is that?

13:00.988 --> 13:02.448
It's a pacifier.

13:02.531 --> 13:04.700
Don't say that as if it's just a mask!

13:04.783 --> 13:06.744
Sorry for freaking you out.

13:06.827 --> 13:11.373
I actually have extreme stage fright, but
when I turn into a baby, it calms me down.

13:11.457 --> 13:13.375
He's calmly saying the craziest nonsense!

13:13.959 --> 13:18.088
The underworld's full of weirdos,
but this guy's really something else.

13:18.172 --> 13:19.298
Oh yeah, he's out there.

13:19.381 --> 13:23.802
Anyway, can we talk
about what I wrote in the letter?

13:23.886 --> 13:26.764
Uh, right, well,
I'm already dating Ogami, so...

13:26.847 --> 13:28.140
I know.

13:28.224 --> 13:30.059
But I still have to say it.

13:31.018 --> 13:32.186
It was love at first sight.

13:32.269 --> 13:33.187
Huh?

13:33.270 --> 13:34.647
I really like you!

13:35.147 --> 13:36.482
Wow, pushy much?

13:36.982 --> 13:38.817
I know you already have a boyfriend.

13:38.901 --> 13:41.153
Even so, will you give me a chance?

13:42.613 --> 13:45.783
Looking at him again,
his eyes really are beautiful.

13:45.866 --> 13:48.994
When he looks at you like that,
your heart skips a beat.

13:49.578 --> 13:53.249
It's not just that his features
are handsome.

13:53.332 --> 13:56.710
There's this almost hypnotic kind
of sex appeal to him.

13:57.336 --> 14:00.172
Except he's got a pacifier in his mouth!

14:00.756 --> 14:04.134
Well, okay, there are like ten different
things I could say here, but...

14:04.218 --> 14:05.052
Hey!

14:05.803 --> 14:08.556
Quit talking out of your ass, moron!

14:09.890 --> 14:13.018
For starters, you don't even like me
that much, do you?

14:13.602 --> 14:16.063
I'm not saying
love at first sight never happens,

14:16.146 --> 14:18.524
and sure, sometimes things move fast
out of nowhere.

14:18.607 --> 14:19.942
But this isn't that.

14:20.025 --> 14:23.320
What ticks me off is that it feels
like you're being made to do this!

14:23.904 --> 14:25.406
Yeah, it's rough dealing with confessions,

14:25.489 --> 14:27.783
but if someone tells me
how they really feel,

14:27.867 --> 14:30.202
I make a point
of giving them a real answer.

14:30.286 --> 14:32.663
But if somebody comes at me
with some joke of a confession,

14:32.746 --> 14:34.748
like they're making fun
of other people's feelings,

14:34.832 --> 14:36.250
I make a point of decking them!

14:37.543 --> 14:38.669
What a...

14:41.005 --> 14:43.340
What a direct, strong person!

14:44.216 --> 14:45.593
I'm really in love!

14:48.387 --> 14:49.680
Good boy, good boy.

14:49.763 --> 14:53.934
If a girl like this did that for me,
I could die happy!

14:54.685 --> 14:55.811
What?

14:55.895 --> 14:57.146
No, sorry!

14:57.229 --> 14:58.439
I'm really sorry!

14:59.023 --> 15:00.733
You were totally right about all of it.

15:01.317 --> 15:03.736
And I like you. For real this time.

15:03.819 --> 15:06.780
If you can tell when someone's lying,
you can also tell when they mean it.

15:08.115 --> 15:09.950
So, anyway, your boyfriend...

15:10.034 --> 15:11.201
Ogami.

15:11.285 --> 15:12.786
"Ogami," right.

15:14.705 --> 15:15.789
- Huh?
- Just like that?

15:17.750 --> 15:18.667
He got behind me?

15:18.751 --> 15:21.086
You're in the business, too, aren't you?

15:21.170 --> 15:25.090
I never thought a sudden confession
like that would actually work.

15:25.591 --> 15:29.553
My plan was to make an impression first,
then ease into it little by little.

15:29.637 --> 15:30.471
But...

15:31.055 --> 15:31.972
I changed my mind.

15:34.141 --> 15:36.685
Putting Noren's position
as fiancée on the line,

15:36.769 --> 15:38.187
I challenge you to a duel.

15:38.270 --> 15:39.563
Huh? A duel?

15:40.064 --> 15:40.981
That.

15:41.649 --> 15:45.569
That fountain pen is proof
of who is the official fiancé.

15:46.695 --> 15:50.616
And if a duel is issued,
it has to be accepted.

15:51.408 --> 15:53.994
The guidelines
have already been announced.

15:54.078 --> 15:55.788
Wait, what is that supposed to mean?

15:55.871 --> 15:57.206
Since when?

15:57.790 --> 16:00.668
If you lose, does that mean
the boyfriend role changes hands?

16:00.751 --> 16:04.421
Jeez! This just keeps getting
more and more annoying!

16:05.130 --> 16:08.509
So, basically, you decided you wanted
to steal her quick and easy, huh?

16:08.592 --> 16:09.593
Exactly.

16:09.677 --> 16:11.345
SIGH...

16:11.428 --> 16:13.555
Please give Noren to me.

16:13.639 --> 16:16.475
I don't give a damn about duels
or whatever else.

16:16.558 --> 16:18.686
But I'm not handing Noren over!

16:18.769 --> 16:20.604
You're way too freaky for your own good.

16:21.188 --> 16:25.609
So, whoever's holding the fountain pen
at the end is the fiancé,

16:25.693 --> 16:26.986
is that it?

16:27.069 --> 16:28.612
That is brutal!

16:28.696 --> 16:30.155
Hang in there, Oga!

16:30.239 --> 16:31.573
This is no laughing matter!

16:31.657 --> 16:34.034
Noren, are you okay?

16:34.118 --> 16:36.286
No, I am not okay!

16:36.370 --> 16:39.581
I hate the idea of people making this
huge spectacle out of fighting over me!

16:39.665 --> 16:40.833
I feel like I'm gonna puke!

16:41.500 --> 16:45.129
And Ogami's only doing this
because I asked him to fake it.

16:45.212 --> 16:48.382
It's not like I was planning
to date anyone in the first place!

16:48.465 --> 16:49.550
Ogami...

16:50.134 --> 16:51.635
It's okay, Master.

16:52.302 --> 16:54.138
I'm in this now.

16:54.221 --> 16:56.890
I'm not gonna lose
no matter what kind of match this is.

16:59.268 --> 17:01.687
They're saying it's a duel
over Noren Mitsuoka!

17:01.770 --> 17:03.605
The one that was posted online?

17:03.689 --> 17:05.899
No way! They're really doing it?

17:05.983 --> 17:07.901
The match lasts one hour.

17:07.985 --> 17:10.738
My objective is to make you
put this pacifier in your mouth.

17:10.821 --> 17:14.241
If you can escape without having it
crammed in, then you win.

17:15.284 --> 17:16.285
Paci... fier!

17:17.036 --> 17:18.454
What kind of stupid contest is this?

17:18.537 --> 17:20.748
A pacifier? What?

17:20.831 --> 17:21.999
I don't get it!

17:22.082 --> 17:24.585
Why is he sucking on one
in the first place?

17:24.668 --> 17:26.545
I love you, Noren.

17:27.129 --> 17:28.338
I really mean it.

17:28.839 --> 17:31.091
So, if I win this duel...

17:31.675 --> 17:33.177
I want to use your lap...

17:33.260 --> 17:34.178
Good boy, good boy.

17:34.261 --> 17:35.262
...as a pillow.

17:35.345 --> 17:36.597
Sorry. Not happening.

17:39.808 --> 17:41.143
Let's get started.

17:41.727 --> 17:44.521
When the last grain falls,
exactly one hour will have passed.

17:44.605 --> 17:46.523
Yeah, yeah, let's do this already.

17:46.607 --> 17:47.566
Begin!

17:51.445 --> 17:52.404
Boss!

17:52.488 --> 17:54.406
Even bracing myself, that was close.

17:54.490 --> 17:57.034
Weirdo factor aside,
his skills are the real deal.

17:57.743 --> 17:58.619
It started!

17:58.702 --> 17:59.870
Oh man!

18:02.539 --> 18:04.333
Uh, isn't this plain bad?

18:04.416 --> 18:07.086
Trying to run away
without blowing your cover and all!

18:07.169 --> 18:08.587
In other words, for one full hour...

18:09.171 --> 18:11.298
I've gotta dodge his attacks
in the most pathetic way possible!

18:11.381 --> 18:12.674
In a weird way, that's kind of pro!

18:16.303 --> 18:17.137
Was that luck?

18:17.721 --> 18:19.098
He's actually managing to dodge him!

18:19.681 --> 18:21.558
Even before I had this younger body,

18:21.642 --> 18:24.019
it'd been a long time
since I'd faced anyone this good.

18:24.103 --> 18:25.562
He's really strong.

18:25.646 --> 18:26.939
Which is exactly why

18:27.481 --> 18:29.775
a match where I lose
if he gets a pacifier in my mouth...

18:29.858 --> 18:30.984
What the hell?

18:35.864 --> 18:37.574
Shh!

18:43.455 --> 18:45.999
After Noren turned me down,
I thought about it.

18:46.083 --> 18:48.585
What exactly is the difference between us?

18:49.294 --> 18:50.921
And then it hit me.

18:51.004 --> 18:53.674
One of us is a baby, and one of us...

18:53.757 --> 18:54.675
isn't!

18:54.758 --> 18:56.385
What the hell are you talking about?

19:07.771 --> 19:10.691
Just try putting it in your mouth,
and you'll get why it's so great!

19:10.774 --> 19:12.943
And once we're both babies...

19:13.443 --> 19:14.903
I'll be superior!

19:14.987 --> 19:17.364
No good! I still have no idea
what you're on about!

19:18.740 --> 19:22.327
But, more than anything,
I'm in love with Noren!

19:22.911 --> 19:25.455
Are your feelings for her
stronger than mine?

19:26.331 --> 19:28.125
My feelings for Noren...

19:28.208 --> 19:29.168
My...

19:30.210 --> 19:31.128
Nope.

19:31.211 --> 19:32.588
Not even one millimeter.

19:32.671 --> 19:33.881
I'm a grown man.

19:34.464 --> 19:37.384
I only took this on because
I got stubborn and dug in my heels.

19:39.052 --> 19:41.638
So, if I lose, worst case,
it can't be helped.

19:41.722 --> 19:42.890
Is that all this is?

19:47.352 --> 19:49.229
TO PAPA

19:49.313 --> 19:50.147
Papa!

19:50.731 --> 19:52.274
No. Wrong.

19:53.358 --> 19:54.693
It's more than that.

19:56.612 --> 19:58.113
About one minute left?

20:00.699 --> 20:02.367
- There they are!
- Over there!

20:06.371 --> 20:07.414
He threw it!

20:07.497 --> 20:08.498
Huh? Is it over?

20:08.582 --> 20:11.001
Yeah, this ends it.

20:11.084 --> 20:12.085
Except...

20:18.258 --> 20:20.928
I never said that was the only pacifier.

20:21.011 --> 20:22.179
A trap!

20:22.262 --> 20:24.264
A whole bunch of them are flying at him!

20:29.978 --> 20:32.481
He left me an escape route on purpose!

20:33.523 --> 20:35.484
He's gonna land on a rake!

20:35.567 --> 20:36.985
Where, if you step on it...

20:37.069 --> 20:39.321
...the handle whips up
and smacks you right in the face!

20:39.905 --> 20:42.074
And there's a pacifier
attached to the end of it!

20:42.157 --> 20:46.328
- And he can't block it!
- It's going in his mouth for sure!

20:47.162 --> 20:48.080
Wha...

20:50.457 --> 20:51.500
It stopped!

20:51.583 --> 20:52.709
How?

20:58.590 --> 21:00.634
So, when he jumped back

21:01.218 --> 21:05.347
he'd already thrown
the wood carving knives?

21:07.224 --> 21:09.226
He made it the whole hour!

21:09.309 --> 21:10.894
How'd he do that at the end?

21:10.978 --> 21:12.646
Ogami wins!

21:13.689 --> 21:14.773
Unbelievable!

21:15.274 --> 21:16.400
My love...

21:16.984 --> 21:18.235
actually lost!

21:19.236 --> 21:20.320
Sorry.

21:20.862 --> 21:23.365
I don't know if mine's
stronger than yours,

21:24.199 --> 21:27.035
but I've got feelings for Noren, too.

21:27.911 --> 21:29.621
They're just nothing like yours.

21:31.623 --> 21:32.874
I only just realized it.

21:33.750 --> 21:37.879
I'd been projecting Kozue onto Noren.

21:38.463 --> 21:40.632
All the things I couldn't do for Kozue...

21:41.550 --> 21:43.385
Maybe it's just self-satisfaction.

21:43.468 --> 21:48.098
Even so, I don't want Noren
to end up unhappy.

23:22.150 --> 23:24.736
Yeah, he's definitely pretty down.

23:26.238 --> 23:28.865
But I don't know how to deal
with two boys dueling over me, either.

23:28.949 --> 23:29.866
HOME EC ROOM

23:29.950 --> 23:32.619
Um, our new club member is...

23:33.245 --> 23:35.122
Shin Kohazame.

23:35.705 --> 23:36.456
Hey!

23:36.540 --> 23:38.834
I'm not giving up, Noren!

23:38.917 --> 23:40.919
Uh, no, please do give up.
